error[B0223]: this call can throw, and it is not marked with `try`
 --> check/try_covers_right.bloom:4:43
  |
4 | public func bad(_ a: Int) throws -> Int { g(a) + (try h(a)) }
  |                                           ^^^^ a throwing call
  |
help: write `try` before it (`try?` for `none` on an error, `do { try … } catch { … }` to handle it)
  = docs: https://github.com/OxyHQ/Bloom/blob/main/docs/bloom-lang-spec.mdx#6-expressions-and-control-flow

error[B0223]: this call can throw, and it is not marked with `try`
 --> check/try_covers_right.bloom:5:51
  |
5 | public func bad2(_ a: Int) -> Int { (try? g(a) ?? h(a)) ?? 0 }
  |                                                   ^^^^ a throwing call
  |
help: write `try` before it (`try?` for `none` on an error, `do { try … } catch { … }` to handle it)
  = docs: https://github.com/OxyHQ/Bloom/blob/main/docs/bloom-lang-spec.mdx#6-expressions-and-control-flow

error[B0201]: `??` gives a fallback for an optional, and this is `Int`
 --> check/try_covers_right.bloom:5:37
  |
5 | public func bad2(_ a: Int) -> Int { (try? g(a) ?? h(a)) ?? 0 }
  |                                     ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^ never `none`
  |
help: remove `?? …`: the value is always there
  = docs: https://github.com/OxyHQ/Bloom/blob/main/docs/bloom-lang-spec.mdx#45-enums-option-and-result
